<section class="hero-desc">
  <h1 class="hero-tagline">UX/UI designer who makes complex products feel simple — from research to developer handoff.</h1>
  <p class="hero-bio">
    Two years into my engineering career at Cross4Channel, I kept noticing the same pattern: the hardest conversations weren't about how to build something — they were about what it should actually do. I was already contributing to UX decisions, so the move to design felt less like a pivot and more like following where my attention was already going.
  </p>
  <p class="hero-bio">
    I work from research to handoff — user interviews, flow mapping, wireframing, high-fidelity design, usability testing. My engineering background means I understand implementation constraints and design things that are feasible to build.
  </p>
</section>

